WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:15.321
This lesson shows you how to prepare an approved image, upload it to the WordPress Media Library, write useful alt text, place it in the correct content item, save safely, and verify the public result without deleting media that another page may still use.

2
00:00:15.671 --> 00:00:21.960
You need an Editor or Administrator account. Editor is enough for routine image uploads and placement.

3
00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:31.578
Do not delete existing media, install image tools, change upload settings, or use an Administrator account merely because an upload or menu looks different.

4
00:00:31.928 --> 00:00:38.400
Gather the one approved final image. Confirm its subject, permission, crop, and web-ready size.

5
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:46.849
Never upload private records, unlicensed images, screenshots containing personal information, or a file you cannot identify.

6
00:00:46.849 --> 00:00:50.664
Stop when the image source or intended use is uncertain.

7
00:00:51.014 --> 00:00:57.627
Open Media, then Library, and select Add New Media File. Upload only the approved final image.

8
00:00:57.627 --> 00:01:05.576
Do not upload several guesses for someone else to sort out. One clear asset is easier to find, use, and maintain.

9
00:01:05.926 --> 00:01:09.516
Rename the file on the computer before uploading it.

10
00:01:09.516 --> 00:01:14.555
Use short lowercase words separated by hyphens that describe the subject.

11
00:01:14.555 --> 00:01:18.904
Avoid names such as final-final, image-one, or a camera number.

12
00:01:18.904 --> 00:01:23.323
Keep the correct file extension, such as J P G, P N G, or Web P.

13
00:01:23.673 --> 00:01:30.119
Select the exact approved file. Wait until the progress indicator finishes and the attachment appears.

14
00:01:30.119 --> 00:01:33.153
If WordPress reports an error, stop and read it.

15
00:01:33.153 --> 00:01:39.599
Do not click repeatedly or upload the same file with different names, because that creates duplicates.

16
00:01:39.949 --> 00:01:47.782
Open the attachment details and write alt text that describes the important subject or purpose in one short phrase or sentence.

17
00:01:47.782 --> 00:01:51.606
Leave alt text empty only when the image is purely decorative.

18
00:01:51.606 --> 00:01:55.800
Do not copy the filename or stuff keywords, locations, and services.

19
00:01:56.150 --> 00:02:00.525
Give the Media Library item a readable title so staff can identify it.

20
00:02:00.525 --> 00:02:04.836
Add a caption only when words should appear publicly under the image.

21
00:02:04.836 --> 00:02:08.898
Use Description only when the site process specifically needs it.

22
00:02:08.898 --> 00:02:12.272
A caption is public content, not a private staff note.

23
00:02:12.622 --> 00:02:17.128
Open the exact page, post, event, or practitioner and its image control.

24
00:02:17.128 --> 00:02:24.200
Choose the uploaded image by its thumbnail and title. Use the intended size and preserve the natural proportions.

25
00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:28.269
Do not drag the image wider or taller in a way that stretches it.

26
00:02:28.619 --> 00:02:34.635
Upload an approved replacement as a new file unless Blue Nova provides a verified replacement tool.

27
00:02:34.635 --> 00:02:37.734
Update the exact content item to use the new image.

28
00:02:37.734 --> 00:02:44.175
Do not delete the old Media Library file, because another page or an older link may still use its address.

29
00:02:44.525 --> 00:02:51.252
Review the crop, alt text, and placement. Select Save or Update one time and wait for confirmation.

30
00:02:51.252 --> 00:02:54.446
Clear only the applicable page or record cache.

31
00:02:54.446 --> 00:03:00.561
Do not purge unrelated content and do not change image, cache, plugin, or server settings.

32
00:03:00.911 --> 00:03:02.723
Open the exact public page.

33
00:03:02.723 --> 00:03:09.099
Confirm the correct image loads, remains sharp, and is not stretched, blurry, or cropped badly.

34
00:03:09.099 --> 00:03:12.387
Check it at phone size and test any linked image.

35
00:03:12.387 --> 00:03:17.823
A successful Media Library upload does not prove the public placement is correct.

36
00:03:18.173 --> 00:03:31.264
Always finish by uploading one approved file, adding useful alt text, placing it in the exact content item, saving once, clearing only the applicable cache, and verifying the public image on desktop and phone.

37
00:03:31.264 --> 00:03:35.774
Stop and contact Blue Nova before deleting or replacing uncertain media.
